<title>UK: NatWest unit sets 10 billion yen five-year bond.</title>
<headline>NatWest unit sets 10 billion yen five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Sanwa International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   NATWEST MARKETS AUSTRALIA LTD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  NATIONAL WESTMINSTER BANK PLC.</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    *1.2	 MATURITY  **12.FEB.02</p>
<p> TYPE   STEP-UP	 ISS PRICE  100.20    PAY DATE    12.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  20 BP     LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA2/AA    DENOMS (M) 100	 SALE LIM US/UK/JP/AU</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> NOTES     *TILL 12.FEB.98 THEN STEPS-UP TO 1.5 PCT IN YEAR</p>
<p>		TWO, 2.15 PCT IN YEAR THREE, 2.8 PCT IN YEAR FOUR</p>
<p>		AND 3.4 PCT IN YEAR 2002.</p>
<p>	    **PAR CALL ON ALL COUPON DATES.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
